  "finding": "On this benchmark's own from-scratch, correctly-masked/correctly-weighted protocol (NOT the runtime checkpoint), M6 (Set Transformer) substantially outperforms GCN on Task 1 (test F1 0.9736 vs 0.5865) and Task 2 (test accuracy 0.5983 vs 0.5375), and edges out the strongest simple baselines B0 (0.9708) and B2 (0.9174) on Task 1 too. This is a controlled, apples-to-apples comparison (same upstream [rule,iso,lstm] snapshots, same TRAIN/VALIDATION/TEST protocol, same masking contract) -- safe to report as-is, but distinct from both (a) the offline M1-M9 crossdevice benchmark sweep (different training pipeline, C05) and (b) the live runtime M6 checkpoint (which has its own, separately-documented class-weight defect -- see standalone_comparison.json)."
